Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Abstract", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97889635012245*^9, 
  3.978896351879611*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"01d70810-8ee9-4c00-848e-\
4511290397ab"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook extends the Relativity Toolkit (v1.9.0) from general relativity \
into basic gauge theory. We demystify \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauge field\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] by relating it to the familiar concept of reference \
frame. We find that forces arise from choice of gauge, specifically from the \
implied connections. Inertial forces, like centrifugal Coriolis force, arise \
from choosing a rotating reference frame. Fundamental forces, like \
electromagnetic and the weak nuclear forces, arise from choices of internal \
gauge \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]reference frames.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] The \
difference is that no choice of gauge can make fundamental forces go away. \
Gravitational tidal forces arising from geodesic deviation are also \
fundamental in this sense: no choice of reference form can make them go away. \
In all cases, invariance of the physics, aka gauge symmetries, imply \
conservation laws.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.977513712847348*^9, {3.9775178669407883`*^9, 3.977517959906126*^9}, {
   3.977517996418476*^9, 3.977518072452635*^9}, {3.9775181219359083`*^9, 
   3.977518224156801*^9}, {3.9775359524035*^9, 3.977536075585163*^9}, {
   3.97753737910937*^9, 3.977537384309*^9}, {3.97764405920399*^9, 
   3.977644347525126*^9}, {3.977672253563974*^9, 3.977672266570442*^9}, {
   3.977678754525832*^9, 3.977678800149303*^9}, {3.977746420549296*^9, 
   3.977746648340251*^9}, 3.978342864699486*^9, {3.97889635568295*^9, 
   3.978896415349616*^9}, {3.978992354969187*^9, 3.978992577930236*^9}, {
   3.9789927194162817`*^9, 
   3.9789928804301643`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"82ee9929-ed00-4b27-92ab-\
af3c1e2fdfea"],

Cell["\<\
In the \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] (up-down) tensorial calculus, we \
implement a new, generalized covariant-derivative operator that handles both \
the spacetime geometry of general relativity via the Christoffel or \
Levi-Civita connection and internal phase geometry of electrodynamic and weak \
gauge connections simultaneously. We validate this engine through four \
automated, symbolic proofs:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.977513712847348*^9, {3.9775178669407883`*^9, 3.977517959906126*^9}, {
   3.977517996418476*^9, 3.977518072452635*^9}, {3.9775181219359083`*^9, 
   3.977518224156801*^9}, {3.9775359524035*^9, 3.977536075585163*^9}, {
   3.97753737910937*^9, 3.977537384309*^9}, {3.97764405920399*^9, 
   3.977644347525126*^9}, {3.977672253563974*^9, 3.977672266570442*^9}, {
   3.977678754525832*^9, 3.977678800149303*^9}, {3.977746420549296*^9, 
   3.977746648340251*^9}, 3.978342864699486*^9, {3.97889635568295*^9, 
   3.978896501376958*^9}, {3.9789925877312517`*^9, 3.9789927027719183`*^9}, 
   3.9789928966541023`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"47ee695d-43a0-4d16-9c62-\
4844153eed24"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Metric Compatibility",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": the Levi-Civita connection is uniquely preserves the metric (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Del]", "g"}], "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "275ce0f6-4484-4eb0-a0af-37f1a9f97f1a"],
 ")"
}], "Item",
