Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Conclusion", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9775359255386477`*^9, 
  3.977535927492813*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8fa93b39-5ef8-4df8-b0c2-\
f43f894f9a34"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this work, we bridge the conceptual and computational gap between \
general relativity and gauge theory. By treating \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauge\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] not just as mathematics but as a concrete choice of \
measurement basis\[LongDash]whether for position in spacetime or phase in a \
complex field\[LongDash]we unify the origin of forces under a single slogan: ",
 StyleBox["Forces arise from connections on sections of principal bundles",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978896777019384*^9, 
  3.9788968560050497`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3a4f8ed0-a4b7-47ca-8202-\
d5acb74b1694"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We show that \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]garbage terms\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
generated by differentiating a phase-shifted field are mathematically \
analogous to \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]garbage terms\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
generated by differentiating a vector in curvilinear coordinates. In both \
cases, a connection field\[LongDash]the vector potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["A", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "71eb9786-dbbd-435d-b305-336b0bf11538"],
 "\:200b or the Christoffel Symbol ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Mu]"}]], 
    RowBox[{"\[Nu]", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Lambda]"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"105a792c-9bbe-4c9f-8e23-e64e8aa29aff"],
 "\[LongDash]cancels these terms and restores phase covariance and \
geometrical covariance, respectively."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978896777019384*^9, 
  3.978896978363305*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"72a831db-f710-493a-a1d1-\
60b557628042"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Computationally, the Relativity Toolkit v1.9.0 is now \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]doubly covariant.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] It \
automatically produces identities for hybrid objects like the Charged Vector \
Boson ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["W", 
    RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Alpha]"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"b0159e98-6c38-4a2b-bb80-6e6932744798"],
 ", which \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]ride on\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] spacetime \
geometry while twisting in an internal gauge space. This confirms that our \
symbolic machinery is ready for more of the Standard Model."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978896777019384*^9, 
  3.9788970527324877`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"07eca9ed-221b-4fed-94d3-\
0423d462a1ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "While this notebook focuses on the Abelian (commutative) ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"U", 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "440502b4-7e35-4d53-9ae7-c5842c07620a"],
 " sector, the geometric machinery sets the stage for generalization to \
non-Abelian gauge theories incorporating ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"SU", 
    RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "102c122a-fe63-4307-9fd2-95c419756e31"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"SU", 
    RowBox[{"(", "3", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "82084809-a5d9-4825-821a-234ae32d4154"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978896777019384*^9, 3.9788971243245983`*^9}, {
  3.978996668022807*^9, 
  3.9789966685824623`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"71164638-8cd3-4ec1-89ec-\
7089b4c54f19"]
}, Open  ]],

